 # VastGaussian
 
-Also called: Block-Based Partitioning, Large-Scale 3DGS via Block Partitioning
 
 ## Overview
-VastGaussian is a large-scale 3D Gaussian Splatting method that partitions a scene into spatially-disjoint regions to handle physical memory limits and varying lighting conditions [S2, unofficial][S4]. It solves the scalability problem of training and rendering millions of Gaussians by training independent models per block and merging them at rendering time with feathered overlap [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike standard grid-based voxelization, it uses a block-based partitioning strategy that allows for decoupled appearance handling, making it suitable for large outdoor scenes with varying illumination [S2, unofficial].
